    "title": "Miami Dolphins sign cornerback Miles Battle",
    "text": "The Miami Dolphins have signed cornerback Miles Battle, the team announced on February 11, 2026.\nBattle played in six games over two seasons with the New England Patriots from 2024 to 2025. During his time there, he made five solo tackles and defended three passes. He entered the NFL as an undrafted free agent with the Kansas City Chiefs in 2024.\nIn college, Battle finished his career at Utah in 2023. That season, he appeared in 13 games with two starts and recorded 32 tackles, including 23 solo tackles, one interception, and four passes defensed. Before transferring to Utah, Battle spent five seasons at Ole Miss from 2018 to 2022. While at Ole Miss, he played in 46 games with four starts and posted a total of 65 tackles (38 solo), two interceptions, eighteen passes defensed, one forced fumble, and one fumble recovery.",
